TITLE:: Parameter
SUMMARY:: Defines a named parameter, type expectation, and validation constraints for a Command.
CATEGORIES:: Control
RELATED:: Classes/Command, Classes/CommandPrompt

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::Parameter:: defines a parameter that a LINK::Classes/Command:: accepts, specifying its expected type (e.g. LINK::Classes/Integer::, LINK::Classes/Float::, LINK::Classes/SimpleNumber::, LINK::Classes/Symbol::, LINK::Classes/String::), whether it accepts a scalar or array of values, and optional value constraints (such as a validation LINK::Classes/Function:: or collection of allowed values).

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a new TELETYPE::Parameter::.

ARGUMENT:: name
A LINK::Classes/String:: or LINK::Classes/Symbol:: naming the parameter.

ARGUMENT:: type
A LINK::Classes/Class:: specifying the expected argument type.

ARGUMENT:: isArray
A LINK::Classes/Boolean:: indicating whether the parameter accepts a space-separated array of values (defaults to CODE::false::).

ARGUMENT:: constraint
An optional validation LINK::Classes/Function:: returning a boolean, or a LINK::Classes/Collection:: of allowed values.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::Parameter:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: constraint
Returns the constraint function or collection, if specified.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/Function::, LINK::Classes/Collection::, or CODE::nil::.

METHOD:: isArray
Returns whether this parameter expects an array of values.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/Boolean::.

METHOD:: isValid
Parses and validates a raw input string.

ARGUMENT:: string
The raw string to parse and validate.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/Boolean::.

METHOD:: name
The name of the parameter.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/String::.

METHOD:: parse
Parses a raw input string into the expected type (or array of values).

ARGUMENT:: string
The raw string to parse.

RETURNS::
The parsed value, or CODE::nil:: if parsing fails.

METHOD:: type
The expected LINK::Classes/Class:: for this parameter.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/Class::.

METHOD:: validate
Validates a previously parsed value against type and constraint rules.

ARGUMENT:: parsedValue
The parsed value to validate.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/Boolean::.

PRIVATE:: init, prParseSingle, prStringIsFloat
